 J.E. Ferrell Jr., and T. Meyer. <year>2005</year>. STIM is a Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> sensor essential for Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>-store-depletion-triggered Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> influx. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>1235</fpage>&#x02013;1241.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16005298</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, D.M., and D.J. Adams. <year>2001</year>. Ionic selectivity of native ATP-activated (P2X) receptor channels in dissociated neurones from rat parasympathetic ganglia. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>534</volume>:<fpage>423</fpage>&#x02013;435.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11454961</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Malayev, A., and D.J. Nelson. <year>1995</year>. Extracellular pH modulates the Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> current activated by depletion of intracellular Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup> stores in human macrophages. <source>J. Membr. Biol.</source> <volume>146</volume>:<fpage>101</fpage>&#x02013;111.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7563033</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">McCleskey, E.W., and W. Almers. <year>1985</year>. The Ca channel in skeletal muscle is a large pore. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>82</volume>:<fpage>7149</fpage>&#x02013;7153.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2413461</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Neher, E., and C.F. Stevens. <year>1977</year>. Conductance fluctuations and ionic pores in membranes. <source>Annu. Rev. Biophys. Bioeng.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>345</fpage>&#x02013;381.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">68708</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Nimigean, C.M., and C. Miller. <year>2002</year>. Na<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> block and permeation in a K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel of known structure. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>120</volume>:<fpage>323</fpage>&#x02013;335.<pub-